<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Mingshu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1965</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Mingshu was a Chinese general from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a> and a former commander of the Nineteenth Route Army. Breaking with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>, he joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-jishen">Li Jishen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cai-tingkai">Cai Tingkai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiang-guangnai">Jiang Guangnai</a> in proclaiming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> People's Government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a> in November 1933, which Nationalist forces suppressed in January 1934. He later sided with the Communists and was condemned as a rightist in 1957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chen-mingshu.jpg" alt="Chen Mingshu" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%99%88%E9%93%AD%E6%9E%A2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
